# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages headers.
#
# The app is a graph of ES modules. If a browser reuses a cached old
# module next to a freshly downloaded new one, the app fails to start —
# so every app file is revalidated (`no-cache` = "ask first", answered
# with a cheap 304 when unchanged). See dev.py for the full story.

/*.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/*.css
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/*.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
